The hour hand travels a total of $2^{\circ \cdot 12}$ in $3$ hours since the hour hand travels $1^{\circ \cdot 12}$ in $60$ minutes. The perimeter of the circle-polygon in which the hour hand must travel is $2\pi(\frac{6}{12}\cdot 8)=8\pi$. Thus the distance traveled by the hour hand in $3$ hours is $\frac{(2^{\circ \cdot 12})(8pi)}{360}=\frac{256\pi}{360}=\frac{16\pi}5$.
